# Find Problems's Fix all on a messy mesh (foirgairwolf on Discord: "the problematic mesh info still occurs" after Fix): a
# blocky remesh-like surface whose cells touch along edges. Fix all leaves no non-manifold edge; the one hole it
# opens (a pinched solid) is listed under "Not fixed:" with why, and so is the Holes Fix that can't cap it.
run open path=$SCRIPT_DIR/../data/check_mesh_messy.obj
click "Geometry##tool.geometry"
click "Check##mesh_check"
expect_text Non-manifold edges
shot before
click "Fix all##mesh_fix"
expect_status Fixed
expect_status Left: 1 hole left open
expect_text Not fixed:
expect_no_text Non-manifold edges
shot after-fix-all
# Checking again keeps the same rows (and clears the note).
click "Check##mesh_check"
expect_no_text Non-manifold edges
expect_no_text Not fixed:
click "Fix##mesh_fix_holes"
expect_status Nothing fixed: 1 hole couldn't be capped
expect_text Not fixed:
shot after-holes-fix
# 200% (the 2880 run's shot is 1440 px of UI): the note wraps inside the tray. Shots only.
ui_scale 200
wait 0.3
shot after-holes-fix-200
ui_scale 100
key ctrl+z
click "Check##mesh_check"
expect_text Non-manifold edges
